    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Error Handling Approaches\n\n**1. INLINE VALIDATION**\n* Use IF nodes to check data\n* Route bad data to error handling\n* Prevents errors before they occur\n\n**2. CONTINUE ON ERROR**\n* Node setting: Continue on Fail\n* Workflow continues despite errors\n* Useful for batch processing\n\n**3. ERROR WORKFLOW**\n* Separate workflow with Error Trigger\n* Catches all workflow failures\n* Centralized error management\n\n**REFERENCE:**\nhttps://docs.n8n.io/flow-logic/error-handling/",
        "height": 520,
        "width": 420,
        "color": 4
      },
      "id": "2b9634ac-718d-462a-bf77-aadd58982881",
      "name": "Error Handling Concept",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        0,
        -160
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Friendly Error Messages\n\n**BEST PRACTICES:**\n* Use clear, non-technical language\n* Include context: what, when, where\n* Provide actionable next steps\n* Log errors for later review\n\n**MESSAGE STRUCTURE:**\n1. Alert icon/severity indicator\n2. Brief description of issue\n3. Relevant data (IDs, values)\n4. Timestamp\n5. Action required or contact info\n\n**AVOID:**\n* Technical jargon\n* Stack traces in user messages\n* Vague descriptions\n* No actionable information",
        "height": 520,
        "width": 400,
        "color": 4
      },
      "id": "9adc5f97-a556-4088-a93e-f6f1f2d59570",
      "name": "Friendly Alerts",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        416,
        -160
      ]
    },
